{"id":"chatcmpl-0b49249c-4d58-4d72-a0ef-cab269891c54","object":"chat.completion","created":1795229954,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"When a single-view medical image is insufficient to directly determine a lateralized finding, use domain-specific anatomical rules (e.g., which structure appears anterior vs posterior on a lateral view) to infer laterality. Confirm the inference with an expert/description tool before committing to an answer. The key is translating view-specific landmarks into the laterality the question asks about.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When the image view alone cannot directly show laterality, apply standard anatomical conventions for that view to map visible contours to left/right structures.\",\n    \"Use an expert/description tool to characterize ambiguous features (position, contour, relative height) before selecting among mutually exclusive options.\",\n    \"Prefer reasoning from view-specific landmark rules (anterior/posterior, obscured/visible) over guessing from prevalence or dataset bias.\",\n    \"When options are mutually exclusive and only one image is given, identify the single discriminating visual cue that maps to one option and verify it with a tool.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Radiology single-view interpretation\": \"Recall standard laterality conventions for the given projection (e.g., on a left lateral, the anterior sharp diaphragmatic contour is typically right). Use these rules to convert visible features into the laterality asked.\",\n    \"Ambiguous medical image QA\": \"Ask a domain expert/description tool targeted questions about the specific structure and its position/contour, then map the description to the answer options.\",\n    \"Mutually exclusive option selection\": \"Identify the one visual feature that distinguishes the options, confirm it with a tool, and avoid relying on base rates or guesses.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the image projection/view label and recall its laterality conventions before interpreting structures.\",\n    \"Verify the discriminating feature (e.g., which contour is abnormally high/anterior) with an expert tool before finalizing the answer.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1242,"total_tokens":1638,"completion_tokens":396,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":1242},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":396}}}